Four required headings, in this order: User story, Acceptance criteria, Test
plan, Dependencies. Keep all four and fill them, using "None" where that is the
honest answer.

Every other heading is optional. Drop an optional heading entirely when it has
no content. An empty optional heading is noise, and a story carrying eight
headings for two facts is why the last batch was unreadable.

There is no word cap. Say everything the implementer needs that the code and
the epic do not already say, and cut the padding rather than the content. The
prose rules, the banned punctuation and the placeholder rules are in the
issue-writing reference.
